`generate_github_alternative_url` still builds its agent with `ureq::agent()`, not `base_ureq_agent()`. So when a mirror is configured, the download uses ureq's default config, which has neither the platform verifier nor the explicit env-proxy setup. A user who has both a mirror and a corporate CA is still broken. This PR is the one that's supposed to make every download honour system certs, so the mirror path is a gap in the change.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-bundler/src/utils/http_utils.rs" lines="42-50"}

::suggestion{file="crates/tauri-bundler/src/utils/http_utils.rs" lines="49"}
    .map(|alt_url| (base_ureq_agent(), alt_url))

The `RootCerts::PlatformVerifier` agent is built in three places: `base_ureq_agent()`, the `platform-certs` branch of `crate_latest_version` in tauri-cli, and implicitly the `ureq::get` default in the WebView2 path. `crate_latest_version` also builds its own agent instead of reusing a shared helper, and it doesn't set the proxy explicitly, which the bundler helper does. Clippy will also flag the trailing `return agent;` in `base_ureq_agent` (`needless_return`), which fails CI if clippy runs with `-D warnings`.

In the head version, `generate_github_mirror_url_from_base` also has an unused `github_url` parameter once the `set_path` call is removed, which rustc flags as a warning.

